@startuml
title The closure family: every data type as an algebra instance

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}

component "AnyAlgebra\n(single closed-enum carrier — one Predicate/Domain type)" as Any #DCFCE7

' ── Leaves: scalar algebras ─────────────────────────────────────────────
rectangle "Leaves (scalar EBAs)" as Leaves #DBEAFE {
  component "Int"     as Int    #BFDBFE
  component "Bool"    as Bool   #BFDBFE
  component "Char"    as Char   #BFDBFE
  component "BigInt"  as BigInt #BFDBFE
  component "BigRat"  as BigRat #BFDBFE
  component "Fixed"   as Fixed  #BFDBFE
  component "Float"   as Float  #BFDBFE
  component "Str"     as Str    #BFDBFE
}

' ── Combinators: each is itself an algebra over sub-algebras ─────────────
rectangle "Combinators (each itself an algebra)" as Comb #DCFCE7 {
  component "Product<A>\n(NaryProductAlgebra)" as Product #BBF7D0
  component "Sum<A>\n(SumAlgebra)"             as Sum     #BBF7D0
  component "Bag<A>\n(BagAlgebra)"             as Bag     #BBF7D0
  component "Map<K,V>\n(MapAlgebra)"           as Map     #BBF7D0
  component "List<A>\n(RegexAlgebra)"          as List    #BBF7D0
  component "Tree<A>\n(TreeAlgebra)"           as Tree    #BBF7D0
}

Any --> Leaves : unifies
Any --> Comb : unifies

' combinators compose sub-algebras
Product ..> Any : sub-algebras
Sum ..> Any : summands
Bag ..> Any : element algebra
Map ..> Any : key × value
List ..> Any : element algebra
Tree ..> Any : payload + children (recursive)

note bottom of Comb
  Each closure is ITSELF a BooleanAlgebra / reject-safe algebra
  ⇒ the SFA/SFT code and the algebra-agnostic proofs are reused
  UNCHANGED. Generalizing "over all data types" = completing the
  family of instances + closing it under type constructors,
  not rewriting the automata. First-order pattern matching
  is subsumed: a pattern lowers to a `TreePred<AnyAlgebra>`.
end note

legend right
|= Color |= Group |
|<#DBEAFE> | scalar leaf algebra |
|<#DCFCE7> | algebra carrier / combinator (itself an algebra) |
endlegend
@enduml
